the-firm-as-one-program-lines-33 : List (List Word)
the-firm-as-one-program-lines-33 = cons "- **N1** Two points carry the most weight." (cons "  C10 is the largest multiplier: checked construction lets AI research scale without trust. S1 is what turns a list of savings into a change in kind. See [C10], [S1]." (cons "- **N2** The bridge to the rationality claim." (cons (quoted (cons "  P1's warrant is the formal form of " (cons "the rational actor cannot be incorrect" (cons ", and that is what C17 runs on. A rational actor concludes P only when it holds a construction of P over every history compatible with what it observed. Where no such construction exists it concludes nothing, so it is never wrong. The language therefore marks exactly what is amenable to rule-based logic: what is derived, what is observed, and what is a stated premise. English could always carry perfect inference for the rational; the language makes that discipline executable and shared. See [P1], [C17]." nil)))) nil)))
